 ## Overview
-Perceptual loss is a regularization term used in differentiable volume rendering to preserve the structural content of the original scene during stylization or inverse rendering tasks [S1, S2]. It operates by minimizing the distance between feature representations of the rendered stylized image and the original captured image in a pre-trained VGG feature space [S1, S2]. Unlike Gram matrix-based style losses that average out details, this method balances stylization and content preservation [S2]. It builds on [Style Loss](11193-style-loss.md).
